  "refinements": {
    "front": "Photographic VOIGTLÄNDER / COLOR-SKOPAR / 35mm F2.5 MC pigment mask; shallow false inscription relief leveled; glass and chrome retained.",
    "rear": "CANON / CAMERA CO., INC. / MADE IN JAPAN / NO. 103959; re-typeset sans-serif engraving matched to measured reference line widths. Typeface is an approximation, not a recovered original font.",
    "top": "Reference Canon 7s wordmark, shutter speed/ASA/DIN face, colored meter window with modeled bezel, 35 film reminder, folding rewind handle, frame counter, film-plane mark and release markings; continuous satin aluminum plate finish.",
    "preservation": "This underside stage retains all 999,829 parent vertex coordinates. Both UV layers, per-corner colors and encoded custom normals are exact on retained faces; 3,578 local underside faces were removed for the recesses. The 22 added detail meshes contain 113,228 triangles. Prior smoothing and inscription refinements remain intact; the compact GLB is a separate derivative with its base plate protected from decimation.",
    "surfaces": "Metal housing, bottom trim and front lens bezel smoothed using virtual-seam Taubin filtering, fitted fascia planes and feathered PBR colors. Barrel markings retained with reduced scan-normal intensity.",
    "bottom": "Reference-matched slotted cap with two spanner holes, offset open 1/4-20 tripod socket, recessed split circular latch with concentric grooves, and two slotted screws. Nominal thread diameter is 6.35 mm and pitch 1.27 mm; the hidden 7 mm blind depth is an estimate, not a measurement recovered from the photograph."
  },
